{"Version":2,"ProgramText":"; \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n;  OLDSCHOOL DEMO\n;\n;  A demo in the style of the Amiga and Atari ST scene: copper bars,\n;  a starfield, a chain of chrome bobs, a bouncing logo and a sine\n;  scroller, all moving on SIN curves, to an eight-channel tune from\n;  the tracker (Sound/Tracker/neon_horizon.amostrk).\n;\n;  Layer 0: copper bars and stars    Layer 1: the bobs\n;  Layer 2: the logo                 Layer 3: the scroll text\n;  The logo and the scroller get their rainbow from RASTER COLOUR:\n;  the raster only shows on the red in the middle of the letters.\n; \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSCREEN 640,480\nTRACK LOAD \"Sound/Tracker/neon_horizon.amostrk\"\nTRACK PLAY\n\n; \u2500\u2500 Layer 0: a dark sky, five copper bars and a starfield \u2500\u2500\nSCREEN SELECT 0\nRASTER CLEAR\nRASTER 1, 0, 0, 480, \"#02020C, #0C0830, #02020C\"\nRASTER 2, 0, 0, 22, \"#200000, #FF5030, #200000\"\nRASTER 3, 0, 0, 22, \"#201000, #FFC030, #201000\"\nRASTER 4, 0, 0, 22, \"#002000, #40FF60, #002000\"\nRASTER 5, 0, 0, 22, \"#000820, #40A0FF, #000820\"\nRASTER 6, 0, 0, 22, \"#180020, #E060FF, #180020\"\nPARTICLE 3, 12\n\n; \u2500\u2500 Layer 1: a chain of chrome bobs \u2500\u2500\nNB = 14\nIMAGE LOAD 1, \"Graphics/Bobs/Chrom/00.png\"\nFOR I = 1 TO NB\n  SPRITE IMAGE I, 1\n  SPRITE HANDLE I, 32, 32\n  SPRITE LAYER I, 1\n  SPRITE ON I\nNEXT I\n\n; \u2500\u2500 Layer 2: the logo, with a rainbow rolling through its red \u2500\u2500\nSCREEN SELECT 2\nFONT LOAD 0, \"Graphics/font.png\", 32, 25\nFONT MAP 0, \"ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ!?:;0123456789@()\u00a3$%.\u2019[]\u201d,-\"\nFONT ZOOM 0, 300\nRASTER 1, 0, 0, 480, \"Red, Orange, Yellow, Green, Cyan, Blue, Magenta, Red\"\nRASTER WRAP 1, TRUE\nRASTER COLOUR 2, \"Red\"\n\n; \u2500\u2500 Layer 3: the sine scroller, in faster copper colours \u2500\u2500\nSCREEN SELECT 3\nFONT LOAD 1, \"Graphics/font.png\", 32, 25\nFONT MAP 1, \"ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ!?:;0123456789@()\u00a3$%.\u2019[]\u201d,-\"\nFONT ZOOM 1, 200\nRASTER 1, 0, 360, 120, \"Yellow, Orange, Red, Magenta, Cyan, Yellow\"\nRASTER COLOUR 3, \"Red\"\n\nTXT$ = \"            HELLO AMIGA AND ATARI FANS!   THIS IS AN OLDSCHOOL DEMO MADE IN AMOS LIKE BASIC.\"\nTXT$ = TXT$ & \"   COPPER BARS, BOBS, A BOUNCING LOGO AND A SINE SCROLLER, ALL ON SIN CURVES.\"\nTXT$ = TXT$ & \"   MUSIC: NEON HORIZON, EIGHT CHANNELS FROM THE TRACKER.   GREETINGS TO EVERYONE WHO EVER\"\nTXT$ = TXT$ & \" WAITED FOR THE VERTICAL BLANK...   WRAP!   \"\nCW = 64          ; a character of the scroller is 64 pixels wide\nSX = 0 : T = 0\n\n; \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nLoop:\n  T = T + 1\n\n  ; The copper bars swing up and down, each a little behind the one before\n  FOR I = 2 TO 6\n    RASTER #0, MOVE I, 229 + SIN(T * 1.6 + I * 26) * 210\n  NEXT I\n\n  ; The bobs follow each other along a Lissajous curve; bigger means nearer\n  FOR I = 1 TO NB\n    A = T * 1.4 - I * 11\n    SPRITE POS I, 320 + SIN(A * 1.3) * 270, 220 + SIN(A * 2.2) * 150\n    SPRITE ZOOM I, 60 + (SIN(A * 0.9) + 1) * 45\n  NEXT I\n\n  ; The logo bounces like a ball and sways from side to side\n  FONT CLEAR\n  LY = 175 - ABS(SIN(T * 2.4)) * 140\n  FONT PRINT #2, 0, 128 + SIN(T * 0.9) * 110, LY, \"AMOS\"\n  RASTER #2, MOVE 1, -((T * 3) MOD 480)\n\n  ; The sine scroller, as on the Amiga: each character is printed on its own, at a height\n  ; from SIN of where it is on the screen. The text runs left and the wave right, so the\n  ; letters roll up and down as they pass through it\n  SX = SX + 4\n  IF SX >= LEN(TXT$) * CW THEN SX = 0\n  C = INT(SX / CW)\n  FOR K = 0 TO 11\n    X = K * CW - (SX MOD CW)\n    FONT PRINT #3, 1, X, 395 + SIN(X * 0.6 - T * 3) * 24, MID$(TXT$ & TXT$, C + 1 + K, 1)\n  NEXT K\n\n  WAIT VBL\nGOTO Loop\n","ScreenWidth":null,"ScreenHeight":null,"Sprites":null,"MapWidth":null,"MapHeight":null,"MapData":null}